162
00:09:37,940 --> 00:09:41,660
So who was keeping the auto industry honest?

163
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:46,260
In 1917, an organization called the Society of Automotive

164
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:51,300
Engineers, or SAE, provided a set of horsepower testing

165
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:53,400
standards.

166
00:09:53,401 --> 00:09:56,700
Back in the early days, they used a very different process

167
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:59,700
from company to company, from tester to tester.

168
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:04,880
What SAE standards tried to do was to establish one formal way

169
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:07,820
of running the test.

170
00:10:07,920 --> 00:10:09,980
From its inception until today,

171
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:12,760
the SAE has tried diligently to make horsepower

172
00:10:12,860 --> 00:10:16,720
a measurement car buyers can believe in.

173
00:10:16,820 --> 00:10:18,720
We look at horsepower.

174
00:10:18,820 --> 00:10:22,360
If a number is stated as SAE-certified power,

175
00:10:22,361 --> 00:10:26,360
that customer has a level of assurance that that's the real

176
00:10:26,361 --> 00:10:30,360
number as tested and as tested properly.

177
00:10:30,361 --> 00:10:33,000
Here at a General Motors facility outside Detroit,

178
00:10:33,001 --> 00:10:37,200
Michigan, technicians are testing an engine to ensure it

179
00:10:37,201 --> 00:10:40,720
performs up to the 310 horsepower they'll advertise

180
00:10:40,721 --> 00:10:44,320
to the public. Millions of dollars are

181
00:10:44,321 --> 00:10:48,360
riding on the results. It's a little nerve-racking.

182
00:10:48,361 --> 00:10:51,360
There's a lot of responsibility involved, and there's a lot of

183
00:10:51,361 --> 00:10:53,020
And there's a lot of things at stake.

184
00:10:53,021 --> 00:10:54,860
So I hope everything runs smoothly,

185
00:10:54,861 --> 00:10:57,200
and I look forward to running it.

186
00:10:57,201 --> 00:10:59,200
An instrument known as a dynamometer

187
00:10:59,201 --> 00:11:03,200
is used to measure the horsepower of the engine.

188
00:11:03,201 --> 00:11:05,200
The engine is mounted to the test stand.

189
00:11:05,201 --> 00:11:07,900
It is then connected through a drive shaft

190
00:11:07,901 --> 00:11:09,680
to our engine dynamometer.

191
00:11:09,681 --> 00:11:12,420
The dynamometer is what actually measures the output

192
00:11:12,421 --> 00:11:14,780
of the engine, measures in horsepower.

193
00:11:14,781 --> 00:11:16,720
The parameters of the dynamometer

194
00:11:16,721 --> 00:11:21,060
are then measured and recorded in the engine control room.

195
00:11:21,061 --> 00:11:23,500
The dynamometer measures horsepower by recording the

196
00:11:23,501 --> 00:11:27,500
torque and rotations of the crankshaft.

197
00:11:27,501 --> 00:11:31,800
The crankshaft is attached to a rotor inside the dynamometer.

198
00:11:31,801 --> 00:11:35,700
As the rotor spins, an electromagnetic field makes

199
00:11:35,701 --> 00:11:38,420
the outside hull of the dynamometer want it turn in the

200
00:11:38,421 --> 00:11:43,220
opposite direction. To measure torque, an arm exerts

201
00:11:43,221 --> 00:11:45,960
resistance force on the dynamometer hull, keeping it

202
00:11:45,961 --> 00:11:48,520
from turning. Out here on the outside,

203
00:11:48,521 --> 00:11:50,620
we have the dynamometer torque arm.

204
00:11:50,621 --> 00:11:54,320
The torque arm is nothing more than a load measuring device.

205
00:11:54,420 --> 00:11:56,660
This load cell down here at the bottom

206
00:11:56,760 --> 00:11:59,160
measures the force exerted, which

207
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:01,340
resists the twisting of the dynamometer

208
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:04,240
as it measures the power.

209
00:12:04,340 --> 00:12:07,640
Car manufacturers still test their own engines.

210
00:12:07,740 --> 00:12:12,780
But since 2005, SAE has required that horsepower tests

211
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:15,840
