227
00:12:51,201 --> 00:12:56,200
Just a slight rattle at certain speeds, which isn't normal.

228
00:12:56,201 --> 00:12:59,200
It could be a loose pin, something wrong with the prop.

229
00:12:59,201 --> 00:13:01,200
We'll check that out.

230
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:09,200
With the witness watching, the GM engineers need to fix the

231
00:13:09,201 --> 00:13:13,200
engineers need to fix the problem fast.

232
00:13:13,300 --> 00:13:15,140
After inspecting the prop shaft,

233
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:17,200
we noticed that the guard was a little bit loose.

234
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:19,140
We then made sure all the bolts were tightened

235
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:21,340
on the prop shaft, make sure all the bolts are tight,

236
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:23,940
and now we're ready to go.

237
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:29,160
With the problem solved, the test continues.

238
00:13:29,260 --> 00:13:32,160
For the next five hours, the engine undergoes

239
00:13:32,260 --> 00:13:34,660
an exhaustive examination.

240
00:13:34,760 --> 00:13:36,000
OK, that was the last test point.

241
00:13:36,100 --> 00:13:37,100
Everything looks good.

242
00:13:37,101 --> 00:13:40,940
Go ahead and start the engine shutdown sequence.

243
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:43,940
With the test completed, the question is,

