258
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:34,860
Inventor James Watt's first steam engines produced six horsepower.

259
00:14:34,861 --> 00:14:39,100
Within 20 years, his engines delivered as much as 190

260
00:14:39,101 --> 00:14:41,160
horsepower.

261
00:14:41,161 --> 00:14:43,960
Horsepower will return on Modern Marvels.

262
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:58,720
They're three-ton boat beasts careening across the water at

263
00:14:58,721 --> 00:15:00,860
speeds exceeding 200 miles per hour.

264
00:15:00,861 --> 00:15:07,660
Their powerful turbine engines generate up to 3,000 horsepower.

265
00:15:07,661 --> 00:15:11,700
This is the world of hydroplane racing.

266
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:21,080
Dave Villwock holds one of the world hydroplane speed records

267
00:15:21,081 --> 00:15:24,480
at 220 miles per hour.

268
00:15:24,481 --> 00:15:29,560
These are a 3,000 horsepower bucking bronco.

269
00:15:29,561 --> 00:15:31,800
Everything about it is difficult to control,

270
00:15:31,900 --> 00:15:34,300
and a lot of times you're not in control.

271
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:40,680
We just try to do the best we can.

272
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:42,900
These craft half skim, half fly

273
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:46,280
across the surface of the water.

274
00:15:46,380 --> 00:15:49,220
Only the propeller is underwater as they throttle

275
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:51,920
to full speed.

276
00:15:52,020 --> 00:15:54,920
A hydroplane is part airplane, part boat.

277
00:15:55,020 --> 00:15:56,860
On my right foot, we have a throttle pedal that

278
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,380
controls the engine throttle.

279
00:15:58,381 --> 00:16:00,720
throttle.

280
00:16:00,820 --> 00:16:03,020
On the left side, we have a flight control pedal,

281
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:06,020
which controls a forward flap that either makes the boat go

282
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:07,020
up or down.

283
00:16:11,020 --> 00:16:13,820
So we're flying the boats like you would an airplane, just

284
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:17,040
very, very close to the water, hopefully.

285
00:16:17,140 --> 00:16:20,740
Hydroplane racing is a summer sport.

286
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:23,240
During the off-season, the boats and engines

287
00:16:23,340 --> 00:16:26,380
go through a complete overhaul.

288
00:16:26,381 --> 00:16:30,820
At the Turban Engine Warehouse near Seattle, Washington,

289
00:16:30,920 --> 00:16:34,380
this engine is fired up to assess that all 3,000 horsepower

290
00:16:34,480 --> 00:16:36,020
will function for the next season.

291
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:46,840
They don't call them thunderboats for nothing.

292
00:16:46,940 --> 00:16:50,140
The extreme noise is deafening.

293
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:52,740
Although it may sound like a jet engine,

294
00:16:52,741 --> 00:16:57,480
It doesn't provide thrust, but rather rotation.

295
00:16:57,580 --> 00:17:01,540
We have rotors that are spinning anywhere from 18,000 revolutions

296
00:17:01,640 --> 00:17:05,280
per minute to 15,000 revolutions per minute for the power

297
00:17:05,380 --> 00:17:06,080
turbines.

298
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:15,000
The turbine engine makes horsepower in four stages,

299
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:20,200
intake, compression, combustion, and exhaust.

300
00:17:20,201 --> 00:17:23,500
That makes a very efficient engine.

301
00:17:23,600 --> 00:17:26,280
In stage one, the turbine engine

302
00:17:26,380 --> 00:17:30,880
takes in air at 300 cubic feet per second.

303
00:17:30,980 --> 00:17:34,680
Stage two, the air goes through a compressor, which

304
00:17:34,780 --> 00:17:38,580
pressurizes it to 90 pounds per square inch.

305
00:17:38,680 --> 00:17:43,220
Stage three, the air is combined with fuel in the burner can

306
00:17:43,320 --> 00:17:45,460
and is ignited.

307
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:49,960
And finally, stage four, the supercharged hot gases

308
00:17:49,961 --> 00:17:52,460
spin the main turbine assembly.

309
00:17:52,461 --> 00:17:54,360
This is the power turbine assembly.

310
00:17:54,361 --> 00:17:56,460
This is where the horsepower is made.

311
00:17:56,461 --> 00:17:59,460
Hot gases that are about 1,500 degrees Fahrenheit

312
00:17:59,461 --> 00:18:01,100
push on all these little blades.

313
00:18:01,101 --> 00:18:03,800
There's lots of gas, lots of little blades.

314
00:18:03,801 --> 00:18:05,600
And this wheel is just like a pinwheel.

315
00:18:05,601 --> 00:18:08,020
All these little blades are at an angle.

316
00:18:08,021 --> 00:18:10,020
It spins this power turbine assembly

317
00:18:10,021 --> 00:18:13,860
15,330 revolutions per minute.

318
00:18:13,861 --> 00:18:15,960
It turns the shaft the same speed.

319
00:18:15,961 --> 00:18:18,260
The shaft is attached to the propeller,

320
00:18:18,261 --> 00:18:20,420
which pushes the race boat forward.

321
00:18:20,520 --> 00:18:22,500
And that's what gives the hydroplane

322
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:26,560
its tremendous speed and horsepower.

323
00:18:26,660 --> 00:18:28,500
With all this explosive horsepower,

324
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:32,400
you might think the engine needs highly combustible fuel.

325
00:18:32,500 --> 00:18:35,480
Everybody thinks that we use exotic fuels in these engines,

326
00:18:35,580 --> 00:18:36,520
but we don't.

327
00:18:36,620 --> 00:18:39,540
What we have is basically home heating

328
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:41,220
oil, which is essentially kerosene.

329
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:47,560
We use kerosene because it's a very stable fuel.

330
00:18:47,561 --> 00:18:50,360
The risk of fire in the boat is very low.

331
00:18:50,460 --> 00:18:52,560
And also, we can extract a lot of energy

332
00:18:52,660 --> 00:18:57,400
out of every gallon of fuel versus a lot of other fuels.

333
00:18:57,500 --> 00:19:01,100
It's one thing to harness 3,000 horsepower on land,

334
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:03,940
but it's quite another on the ever-changing surface of water.

335
00:19:11,580 --> 00:19:13,920
Drivers are put to the ultimate test.

336
00:19:14,020 --> 00:19:16,560
You're essentially an accident waiting to happen.

337
00:19:16,561 --> 00:19:19,460
But you're going so fast, you cover a football field

338
00:19:19,560 --> 00:19:20,560
in a second.

339
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:22,060
So when you're looking for something to happen,

340
00:19:22,160 --> 00:19:24,800
you're looking way down the track.

341
00:19:24,900 --> 00:19:28,100
Ken Muscatel is a hydroplane driver who lost his battle

342
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:31,100
with horsepower in a spectacular crash.

343
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:32,400
Oh, my God.

344
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:40,320
The boat was going good, about 185, not super fast.

345
00:19:40,420 --> 00:19:43,060
And all of a sudden, it just starts lifting.

346
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:44,260
And it's not coming down.

347
00:19:44,261 --> 00:19:46,600
and it goes higher and higher and higher,

348
00:19:46,700 --> 00:19:48,900
probably ended up 60 feet in the air,

349
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,860
flew all the way around 360, landed on its tail,

350
00:19:51,960 --> 00:19:55,700
slapped down back on the water, broke the boat in half,

351
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:56,700
but was kept going.

352
00:19:56,800 --> 00:19:59,000
So I had to shut it off, and I just waited for people to come.

353
00:20:02,020 --> 00:20:04,520
I felt lucky, lucky to be alive.

354
00:20:08,520 --> 00:20:10,760
Lucky not to be hurt, and still disappointed

355
00:20:10,860 --> 00:20:14,260
because we weren't going to be able to race the boat.

356
00:20:14,261 --> 00:20:19,560
So with all the speed and danger, have hydroplanes

357
00:20:19,561 --> 00:20:21,560
reached the outer limits of horsepower?

358
00:20:21,561 --> 00:20:27,200
The bottom line is that in the future of hydroplane racing,

359
00:20:27,201 --> 00:20:33,620
I see more technology, more power, faster race boats.

360
00:20:33,621 --> 00:20:37,220
But high horsepower on water doesn't always

361
00:20:37,221 --> 00:20:41,720
mean high speed. It can also determine

362
00:20:41,721 --> 00:20:43,720
It can also determine sheer muscle.

363
00:20:48,260 --> 00:20:51,900
One of the most powerful diesel engines in the world

364
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:59,840
is the Wartzilla RTA-96C, with an astounding 95,000 horsepower.

365
00:20:59,940 --> 00:21:03,380
This behemoth was designed to power mammoth ships,

366
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:08,080
like the Costco Long Beach, a 72,000-ton cargo container

367
00:21:08,081 --> 00:21:13,760
Manufactured in Korea, the Wartzilla is 76 feet long

368
00:21:13,860 --> 00:21:18,160
and 44 feet high, as large as a three-story house.

369
00:21:20,700 --> 00:21:23,100
I've been working on big engines all my life.

370
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:24,500
This is the biggest.

371
00:21:24,600 --> 00:21:25,600
It's amazing.

372
00:21:25,700 --> 00:21:26,960
It's a challenge.

373
00:21:27,060 --> 00:21:30,100
It's a lot of horsepower to look after.

374
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:31,540
It's a big engine, massive.

375
00:21:34,040 --> 00:21:38,080
The total engine weight is 2,300 tons.

376
00:21:38,081 --> 00:21:42,680
The crankshaft alone weighs 300 tons.

377
00:21:42,780 --> 00:21:48,920
It's over 1,000 times more powerful than many car engines.

378
00:21:49,020 --> 00:21:51,020
Each of the Wartzilla's 12 cylinders

379
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:54,840
delivers 8,000 horsepower.

380
00:21:54,940 --> 00:21:57,740
This is a spare piston for this main engine.

381
00:21:57,840 --> 00:22:02,480
It's 20 feet tall, and it weighs 5 and 1,5 tons.

382
00:22:02,580 --> 00:22:06,480
Just imagine this piston moving up and down the engine at 102

383
00:22:06,481 --> 00:22:08,220
times per minute.

384
00:22:08,320 --> 00:22:11,020
That's incredible.

385
00:22:11,120 --> 00:22:14,420
Inside the 12 assembly units, where the pistons are

386
00:22:14,520 --> 00:22:17,860
connected to the crankshaft, technicians inspect the engine

387
00:22:17,960 --> 00:22:19,660
parts.

388
00:22:19,760 --> 00:22:23,100
Running at full power, the Wartzilla would be far too

389
00:22:23,200 --> 00:22:25,840
dangerous to approach this closely.

390
00:22:25,940 --> 00:22:28,340
So it slowed down to a fraction of its normal speed.

391
00:22:32,340 --> 00:22:34,700
We are slowly turning the engine at the moment.

392
00:22:34,701 --> 00:22:38,240
Just to give you an idea of this massive piece of steel

393
00:22:38,340 --> 00:22:41,900
coming up, driven from the pistons.

394
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:43,840
When this machine is in operation,

395
00:22:43,940 --> 00:22:47,340
you will never be able to stand in this area.

396
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:50,140
However, using time-lapse photography,

397
00:22:50,240 --> 00:22:52,060
we're able to speed up the process

398
00:22:52,160 --> 00:22:55,660
and bring the engine to life.

399
00:22:55,760 --> 00:22:58,360
With each stroke of the 5 1⁄2-ton assembly,

400
00:22:58,460 --> 00:22:59,860
it covers more than 8 feet.

401
00:22:59,861 --> 00:23:03,200
feet.

402
00:23:03,201 --> 00:23:06,560
This enormous mass of metal drives the crankshaft, which

403
00:23:06,561 --> 00:23:09,100
generates the 95,000 horsepower.

404
00:23:13,100 --> 00:23:18,920
The engine consumes up to 250 tons of fuel a day.

405
00:23:18,921 --> 00:23:25,120
It can propel the Costco Long Beach at up to 24 knots, a

406
00:23:25,121 --> 00:23:27,460
a blazing speed for a container ship this size.

407
00:23:30,460 --> 00:23:34,460
It gives you a feeling like a car driver.

408
00:23:34,461 --> 00:23:39,140
If he has a fast car on a good road without speed limit,

409
00:23:39,141 --> 00:23:42,100
where you can use his horsepowers.

410
00:23:42,101 --> 00:23:45,600
So it is a nice feeling.

411
00:23:45,601 --> 00:23:48,620
Because of the rising demand for global shipping,

412
00:23:48,621 --> 00:23:53,040
bigger and faster ships are sure to follow.

413
00:23:53,041 --> 00:23:54,980
In the future, ship engines could pack up

414
00:23:54,981 --> 00:24:01,320
to 115,000 horsepower. Propulsion isn't the only use

415
00:24:01,321 --> 00:24:05,660
for tremendous horsepower. It's also harnessed to generate

416
00:24:05,661 --> 00:24:09,560
electric power. When the lights go out, people's

417
00:24:09,561 --> 00:24:12,300
lives depend on these monstrous engines.

418
00:24:16,140 --> 00:24:19,660
Since the 1980s, most hydroplane races have been won by boats

419
00:24:19,661 --> 00:24:23,460
using a turbine engine originally designed for Vietnam-era

420
00:24:23,461 --> 00:24:28,560
Chinook helicopters. Horsepower will return on Modern

421
00:24:28,561 --> 00:24:29,560
Marvels.

422
00:24:34,780 --> 00:24:40,140
Welcome to Waukesha, Wisconsin, a tranquil, unassuming town

423
00:24:40,141 --> 00:24:44,580
in middle America. However, it's also home

424
00:24:44,581 --> 00:24:53,460
to incredible horsepower. Here at Waukesha Engine.

425
00:24:53,461 --> 00:24:56,000
Many people have maybe never heard the name of Waukesha

426
00:24:56,060 --> 00:24:58,300
Engine, but it's out there producing power

427
00:24:58,360 --> 00:25:00,040
throughout the world.

428
00:25:00,100 --> 00:25:02,600
In this 1 million square foot factory,

429
00:25:02,660 --> 00:25:11,140
more than 800 workers design, build, and ship

430
00:25:11,220 --> 00:25:14,980
mammoth engine generators that deliver essential electric

431
00:25:15,040 --> 00:25:18,280
power around the globe.

432
00:25:18,360 --> 00:25:21,160
One of the largest in the world is the Advanced Power

433
00:25:21,161 --> 00:25:27,160
generation system, or APG3000, which produces 4,400 horsepower.

434
00:25:33,440 --> 00:25:37,180
Waukesha engines are about horsepower, pure and simple.

435
00:25:37,280 --> 00:25:39,240
The way that we get that horsepower

436
00:25:39,340 --> 00:25:41,180
is we throw a lot of iron at it.

437
00:25:41,280 --> 00:25:42,440
The pistons are bigger.

438
00:25:42,540 --> 00:25:44,080
The block is bigger.

439
00:25:44,180 --> 00:25:46,660
The connecting rods, everything's just bigger, beefier

440
00:25:46,760 --> 00:25:48,680
to handle the durability and reliability

441
00:25:48,780 --> 00:25:51,160
that the customers demand.

442
00:25:51,161 --> 00:25:56,760
The APG engine is 11 feet high and 25 feet long,

443
00:25:56,860 --> 00:26:01,540
and it weighs in at a massive 40 tons.

444
00:26:01,640 --> 00:26:06,200
It's a big engine with an even bigger job to perform.

445
00:26:06,300 --> 00:26:08,040
The customers that buy these engines

446
00:26:08,140 --> 00:26:09,880
are in very critical applications.

447
00:26:09,980 --> 00:26:13,440
In a lot of places, we are their only source of electricity,

448
00:26:13,540 --> 00:26:17,260
be it in foreign countries where there is no electrical grid,

449
00:26:17,261 --> 00:26:20,260
be it in hospitals where there's a power outage,

450
00:26:20,360 --> 00:26:23,040
they cannot go down because people's lives

451
00:26:23,140 --> 00:26:26,240
often depend on these engines operating reliably

452
00:26:26,340 --> 00:26:29,140
for as long as they can.

453
00:26:29,240 --> 00:26:31,880
These engines use an internal combustion system

454
00:26:31,980 --> 00:26:34,940
that employs pistons connected to a crankshaft,

455
00:26:35,040 --> 00:26:36,140
much like in a car.

456
00:26:38,720 --> 00:26:43,180
Besides the size, the biggest difference is the fuel.

457
00:26:43,181 --> 00:26:49,020
Instead of gasoline, the APG runs on natural gas.

458
00:26:49,120 --> 00:26:51,580
Natural gas is a very clean burning fuel

459
00:26:51,680 --> 00:26:53,060
and very friendly to the environment,

460
00:26:53,160 --> 00:26:55,060
much more so than gasoline.

461
00:26:55,160 --> 00:26:58,320
It's very plentiful around the world in remote locations,

462
00:26:58,420 --> 00:27:00,840
so it's easily available, and it's definitely

463
00:27:00,940 --> 00:27:02,640
becoming a fuel of the future.

464
00:27:02,740 --> 00:27:07,600
The APG can draw natural gas straight from ground deposits

465
00:27:07,700 --> 00:27:11,240
or even draw methane gas from a garbage landfill.

466
00:27:11,241 --> 00:27:13,740
It always has a steady supply of power

467
00:27:13,840 --> 00:27:17,480
and never has to be refueled.

468
00:27:17,580 --> 00:27:19,520
This combination of engine and generator

469
00:27:19,620 --> 00:27:23,880
is known as an Inginator.

470
00:27:23,980 --> 00:27:26,920
The Inginators are designed to last for years and years.

471
00:27:27,020 --> 00:27:29,620
Most of the major components last for the lifetime

472
00:27:29,720 --> 00:27:30,720
of the engine.

473
00:27:32,660 --> 00:27:35,940
Construction of the APG begins when raw stock

474
00:27:36,040 --> 00:27:37,640
from an iron foundry is delivered.

475
00:27:37,641 --> 00:27:38,341
is delivered.

476
00:27:41,540 --> 00:27:44,920
It'll take up to four weeks before the 8,700 pound crank

477
00:27:44,921 --> 00:27:49,320
case and 3,700 pound crankshaft reach what is known

478
00:27:49,321 --> 00:27:52,680
as engine tolerance.

479
00:27:52,681 --> 00:27:55,260
Tolerances are how close these parts fit together.

480
00:27:55,261 --> 00:27:57,700
They have to seal a lot of pressure from combustion,

481
00:27:57,701 --> 00:27:59,460
and there's a lot of moving parts.

482
00:27:59,461 --> 00:28:01,860
And because you're going through so many cycles,

483
00:28:01,861 --> 00:28:04,340
it's important that they fit to be extremely close.

484
00:28:04,341 --> 00:28:12,940
The crankshaft is holed onto a computerized layer,

485
00:28:13,040 --> 00:28:16,980
where almost a quarter of its size will be shaved off.

486
00:28:17,080 --> 00:28:19,560
We'll be removing 600 pounds from this crankshaft

487
00:28:19,660 --> 00:28:21,360
as it's processed down the line.

488
00:28:21,460 --> 00:28:23,220
We'll be finishing those diameters down

489
00:28:23,320 --> 00:28:24,900
to the width of a human hair.

490
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:27,300
We need this exacting tolerance in order for the engine

491
00:28:27,400 --> 00:28:30,800
to operate properly in the field.

492
00:28:30,900 --> 00:28:34,340
The main part of the engine, the crankcase,

493
00:28:34,341 --> 00:28:38,080
undergoes a process known as machining,

494
00:28:38,180 --> 00:28:40,040
in which computer-assisted cutting tools

495
00:28:40,140 --> 00:28:42,340
drill cylinders for the pistons that will eventually

496
00:28:42,440 --> 00:28:45,460
be installed.

497
00:28:45,560 --> 00:28:48,580
We machine off over 1,500 pounds

498
00:28:48,680 --> 00:28:51,820
to get that piece of iron into the dimensions that we

499
00:28:51,920 --> 00:28:55,360
require for quality.

500
00:28:55,460 --> 00:28:58,060
The 42-pound pistons also go through the machining

501
00:28:58,160 --> 00:29:04,340
process until they shine like jewels.

502
00:29:04,341 --> 00:29:07,640
These are aluminum pistons, and when you machine them,

503
00:29:07,740 --> 00:29:10,520
they get the shiny appearance, but don't let that fool you.

504
00:29:10,620 --> 00:29:12,320
When these are in operation in the engine,

505
00:29:12,420 --> 00:29:13,920
it's a very harsh environment.

506
00:29:14,020 --> 00:29:16,280
When you have this combustion, this huge explosion

507
00:29:16,380 --> 00:29:18,260
that goes on in the cylinder, this piston

508
00:29:18,360 --> 00:29:19,860
has to withstand that pressure, which

509
00:29:19,960 --> 00:29:22,760
can be as high as 2,000 pounds per square inch.

510
00:29:22,860 --> 00:29:25,060
And that's what creates your horsepower that's

511
00:29:25,160 --> 00:29:27,400
transmitted out the crankshaft.

512
00:29:27,500 --> 00:29:30,840
When all the main engine parts are ready for assembly,

513
00:29:30,841 --> 00:29:33,240
They're placed on a rollover.

514
00:29:33,340 --> 00:29:36,780
It's something like an enormous engine rotisserie.

515
00:29:36,880 --> 00:29:39,420
On the rollover that you see on the assembly line

